{"timestamp":"2026-07-27T19:40:30.500Z","type":"decision","context":"proxy.ts + app/checkout/page.tsx","content":"Redirect bug fix: /checkout gate was implemented as useEffect + sessionStorage.getItem(). This runs client-side after hydration — Next.js SSR serves the full job card HTML before JS executes, so a direct navigation to /checkout with no approvalStatus set would flash the protected content before redirecting. Fixed by moving the gate to proxy.ts (Next.js 16 server-side middleware, renamed from middleware.ts). The proxy reads an approvalStatus cookie set at underwriting approval and issues a 307 redirect before any HTML is generated. Verified: curl -s -D - http://localhost:3000/checkout returns HTTP/1.1 307 with no cookie; returns 200 with cookie.","tags":["checkout-gate","proxy","redirect","ssr","bug-fix","verified"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-27T19:42:27.508Z","type":"milestone","context":"README.md","content":"README written to exact graded structure from brief: what/why/who (multi-sided — ABC Community Bank as buyer, AirConPro as integration partner, CoolAir HVAC as sub-merchant, Arnold Freeze as consumer); APIs used and why (Stripe for card path, mocked routes for underwriting and financing); run locally instructions; product decisions section including PayFac reframe, why financing was added, why stubs are stubbed, redirect bug/fix, and honest session hook limitations; what next section (multi-bank routing, async webhooks, real KYB, fraud scoring, hook discipline); builder context stated plainly and specifically.","tags":["readme","task-13","graded-deliverable"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-27T20:01:28.274Z","type":"milestone","context":"production smoke test — nymbus-cjones.vercel.app","content":"Fresh prod deploy (--force, no cache) after Stripe env vars added to Vercel dashboard. Smoke test results: (1) Success card: POST /api/stripe/create-payment-intent created real PaymentIntent pi_3TxuhxENN4Yp4lBx04GrD8m6, confirmed with pm_card_visa, status=succeeded, amount=800000, metadata jobId=JOB-2024-0847 and customer=Mr. Arnold Freeze correct. (2) Decline card: fresh PI confirmed with pm_card_visa_chargeDeclinedInsufficientFunds, Stripe returned api error message \"Your card has insufficient funds.\" — real Stripe error, not a mocked string. (3) /confirmation?type=card returns HTTP 200. (4) /checkout with no cookie returns 307 redirect to / on prod.","tags":["production","smoke-test","stripe","verified","task-15"]}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-27T20:20:25.320Z","type":"milestone","context":"final consistency and completeness pass","content":"Three fixes: (1) PLANNING_AGENT_OUTPUT.md created from genuine Planning Agent invocation — verbatim output formalizing the two-flow architecture, connector API surface, and PayFac-as-a-Service reframe. Distinct from FEATURE_SPEC.md. (2) Product offering page hero and capability cards rewritten to consistently address the SaaS platform partner audience (\"Our bank, inside your software\" / \"your users get paid\") rather than accidentally pitching to another bank. (3) README updated: KIRO_STARTING_BRIEF.md and PLANNING_AGENT_OUTPUT.md referenced in project structure and product decisions sections. Spec artifact provenance clearly documented.","tags":["planning-agent","product-offering-page","readme","final-pass"]}
